#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"An overview of the available execution modes in Qiskit Runtime, including "
"sessions, batch, and single jobs."
msgstr ""
"Gambaran umum tentang mode eksekusi yang tersedia di Qiskit Runtime, "
"termasuk session, batch, dan single job."

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Introduction to Qiskit Runtime execution modes"
msgstr "Pengantar mode eksekusi Qiskit Runtime"

#. type: Title #
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Introduction to Qiskit Runtime execution modes {#introduction-to-qiskit-"
"runtime-execution-modes}"
msgstr ""
"Pengantar mode eksekusi Qiskit Runtime {#introduction-to-qiskit-runtime-"
"execution-modes}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"When Qiskit Runtime was introduced, users could only execute circuits as "
"individual jobs. As different types of quantum workloads emerged, the need "
"for different scheduling strategies became evident. The execution modes "
"determine how your jobs are scheduled, and choosing the right execution mode"
" allows your workload to run efficiently within your budget. There are three"
" execution modes: job, session, and batch.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ketika Qiskit Runtime pertama kali diperkenalkan, pengguna hanya bisa "
"menjalankan Circuit sebagai job individu. Seiring munculnya berbagai jenis "
"workload kuantum, kebutuhan akan strategi penjadwalan yang berbeda pun "
"menjadi jelas. Mode eksekusi menentukan bagaimana job-job Anda dijadwalkan, "
"dan memilih mode eksekusi yang tepat memungkinkan workload berjalan secara "
"efisien sesuai anggaran yang ada. Ada tiga mode eksekusi: job, session, dan "
"batch.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Job mode {#job-mode}"
msgstr "Mode job {#job-mode}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A single primitive request made without a context manager. Circuits and "
"inputs are packaged as primitive unified blocs (PUBs) and submitted as an "
"execution task on the quantum computer. To run in job mode, specify "
"`mode=backend` when instantiating a primitive. See [Estimator "
"examples](/guides/estimator-examples) and [Sampler "
"examples](/guides/sampler-examples) for usage.\n"
msgstr ""
"Satu permintaan primitif yang dibuat tanpa context manager. Circuit dan "
"input dikemas sebagai primitive unified blocs (PUBs) dan dikirimkan sebagai "
"tugas eksekusi pada komputer kuantum. Untuk menjalankan dalam mode job, "
"tentukan `mode=backend` saat membuat instance primitif. Lihat [Contoh "
"Estimator](/guides/estimator-examples) dan [Contoh Sampler](/guides/sampler-"
"examples) untuk cara penggunaannya.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"batch-mode\"></span>\n"
msgstr "<span id=\"batch-mode\"></span>\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Batch mode {#batch-mode}"
msgstr "Mode batch {#batch-mode}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A multi-job manager for efficiently running experiments comprising multi-job"
" workloads. These workloads are made up of independently executable jobs "
"that have no conditional relationship with each other. With batch mode, "
"users submit their jobs all at once. \n"
msgstr ""
"Manajer multi-job untuk menjalankan eksperimen yang terdiri dari workload "
"multi-job secara efisien. Workload ini terdiri dari job-job yang bisa "
"dieksekusi secara independen tanpa hubungan kondisional satu sama lain. "
"Dengan mode batch, pengguna mengirimkan semua job sekaligus.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The system parallelizes or threads the pre-processing (classical computing) "
"step of each primitive job to more tightly package quantum execution across "
"jobs, and then runs the quantum execution of each job in quick succession to"
" deliver the most efficient results. For further details about threading, "
"see the [Execution mode FAQ page](/guides/execution-modes-faq#parallel).\n"
msgstr ""
"Sistem memparalelkan atau men-thread langkah pra-pemrosesan (komputasi "
"klasik) dari setiap primitive job agar eksekusi kuantum antar job bisa "
"dikemas lebih rapat, lalu menjalankan eksekusi kuantum setiap job secara "
"berurutan cepat untuk memberikan hasil yang paling efisien. Untuk detail "
"lebih lanjut tentang threading, lihat [halaman FAQ mode "
"eksekusi](/guides/execution-modes-faq#parallel).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![A sets of jobs being run in batch mode.  The classical computation part of"
" each job happens simultaneously, then all jobs are sent to the QPU.  The "
"QPU is locked for your use from the time the first job reaches the QPU until"
" the last job is done processing on the QPU.  There is no gap between jobs "
"where the QPU is idle.](/docs/images/guides/execution-modes/batch.svg 'How a"
" batch works')\n"
msgstr ""
"![Sekumpulan job yang dijalankan dalam mode batch. Bagian komputasi klasik "
"dari setiap job terjadi secara bersamaan, lalu semua job dikirim ke QPU. QPU"
" dikunci untuk penggunaan Anda sejak job pertama mencapai QPU hingga job "
"terakhir selesai diproses. Tidak ada jeda antar job di mana QPU "
"menganggur.](/docs/images/guides/execution-modes/batch.svg 'Cara kerja "
"batch')\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Notes\">\n"
"- When batching, jobs are not guaranteed to run in the order they are submitted. Also, while your batch jobs will run as closely together as possible, they don't get exclusive access to the backend. Therefore, your batch jobs might run in parallel with other users' jobs if there is enough processing capacity on the QPU. Additionally, QPU calibration jobs could run between the batched jobs.\n"
"- The queuing time does not decrease for the first job submitted within a batch. Therefore, batches do not provide any benefits when running a single job.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Catatan\">\n"
"- Saat menggunakan batch, urutan eksekusi job tidak dijamin sesuai urutan pengiriman. Selain itu, meskipun job batch Anda akan berjalan sedekat mungkin satu sama lain, mereka tidak mendapatkan akses eksklusif ke Backend. Oleh karena itu, job batch Anda mungkin berjalan bersamaan dengan job pengguna lain jika ada kapasitas pemrosesan yang cukup di QPU. Selain itu, job kalibrasi QPU bisa saja berjalan di antara job batch.\n"
"- Waktu antrean tidak berkurang untuk job pertama yang dikirimkan dalam batch. Oleh karena itu, batch tidak memberikan manfaat apa pun saat menjalankan satu job saja.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To run in batch mode, specify `mode=batch` when instantiating a primitive or"
" run the job in a batch context manager. See [Run jobs in a "
"batch](/guides/run-jobs-batch) for examples.\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk menjalankan dalam mode batch, tentukan `mode=batch` saat membuat "
"instance primitif atau jalankan job dalam batch context manager. Lihat "
"[Jalankan job dalam batch](/guides/run-jobs-batch) untuk contoh-contohnya.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"session-mode\"></span>\n"
msgstr "<span id=\"session-mode\"></span>\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Session mode {#session-mode}"
msgstr "Mode Session {#session-mode}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A dedicated window for running a multi-job workload.  During this window, "
"the user has exclusive access of the system and no other jobs can run - "
"including calibration jobs. This allows users to experiment with variational"
" algorithms in a more predictable way and even run multiple experiments "
"simultaneously, taking advantage of parallelism in the stack. Using sessions"
" helps avoid delays caused by queuing each job separately, which can be "
"particularly useful for iterative tasks that require frequent communication "
"between classical and quantum resources.\n"
msgstr ""
"Window khusus untuk menjalankan workload multi-job. Selama window ini, "
"pengguna mendapat akses eksklusif ke sistem dan tidak ada job lain yang bisa"
" berjalan — termasuk job kalibrasi. Hal ini memungkinkan pengguna "
"bereksperimen dengan algoritma variasional secara lebih terprediksi dan "
"bahkan menjalankan beberapa eksperimen secara bersamaan, memanfaatkan "
"paralelisme dalam stack. Menggunakan Session membantu menghindari penundaan "
"yang disebabkan oleh antrean setiap job secara terpisah, yang bisa sangat "
"berguna untuk tugas iteratif yang memerlukan komunikasi sering antara sumber"
" daya klasik dan kuantum.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![A sets of jobs being run in session mode and the other is being run in "
"batch mode.  Between each job is the interactive TTL (interactive time to "
"live).  The active window starts when the first job starts and ends after "
"the last job is completed. After the final job of the first set of jobs "
"completes, the active window ends and the session is paused (but not "
"closed).  Another set of jobs then starts and jobs continue in a similar "
"manner. The QPU is reserved for your use during the entire "
"session.](/docs/images/guides/execution-modes/session.svg 'How a session "
"works')\n"
msgstr ""
"![Sekumpulan job yang dijalankan dalam mode session dan yang lainnya "
"dijalankan dalam mode batch. Di antara setiap job terdapat interactive TTL "
"(interactive time to live). Active window dimulai saat job pertama mulai "
"berjalan dan berakhir setelah job terakhir selesai. Setelah job terakhir "
"dari set job pertama selesai, active window berakhir dan session dijeda "
"(tetapi tidak ditutup). Serangkaian job lainnya kemudian dimulai dan job "
"terus berjalan dengan cara serupa. QPU dicadangkan untuk penggunaan Anda "
"selama seluruh session berlangsung.](/docs/images/guides/execution-"
"modes/session.svg 'Cara kerja session')\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To run in session mode, specify `mode=session` when instantiating a "
"primitive, or run the job in a session context manager. See [Run jobs in a "
"session](/guides/run-jobs-session) for examples.\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk menjalankan dalam mode Session, tentukan `mode=session` saat membuat "
"instance primitif, atau jalankan job dalam session context manager. Lihat "
"[Jalankan job dalam session](/guides/run-jobs-session) untuk contoh-"
"contohnya.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Notes\">\n"
"- The queuing time does not decrease for the first job submitted within a session. Therefore, sessions do not provide any benefits when running a single job.\n"
"- Open Plan users cannot submit session jobs.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Catatan\">\n"
"- Waktu antrean tidak berkurang untuk job pertama yang dikirimkan dalam session. Oleh karena itu, session tidak memberikan manfaat apa pun saat menjalankan satu job saja.\n"
"- Pengguna Open Plan tidak bisa mengirimkan job session.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Basic workflow {#basic-workflow}"
msgstr "Alur kerja dasar {#basic-workflow}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The basic workflow for batches and sessions is similar:\n"
msgstr "Alur kerja dasar untuk batch dan session serupa:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The first job in a batch or session enters the normal queue. For batches, "
"the entire batch of jobs is scheduled together.\n"
msgstr ""
"Job pertama dalam batch atau session masuk ke antrean normal. Untuk batch, "
"seluruh kumpulan job dijadwalkan bersama.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"When the first job starts running, the maximum time to live (TTL) timer "
"starts, and does not stop or pause until the end is reached.\n"
msgstr ""
"Saat job pertama mulai berjalan, timer maksimum time to live (TTL) dimulai, "
"dan tidak berhenti atau dijeda hingga batas waktu tercapai.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The interactive TTL timer starts after each job is completed.  If there are no workload jobs ready within the interactive TTL window, the workload is temporarily deactivated and normal job selection resumes. A job can reactivate the deactivated workload if the batch or session has not reached its maximum TTL value.\n"
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"The job must go through the normal queue to reactivate the workload.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"Timer interactive TTL dimulai setelah setiap job selesai. Jika tidak ada job workload yang siap dalam window interactive TTL, workload dinonaktifkan sementara dan pemilihan job normal dilanjutkan. Sebuah job bisa mengaktifkan kembali workload yang dinonaktifkan jika batch atau session belum mencapai nilai TTL maksimumnya.\n"
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"Job harus melalui antrean normal untuk mengaktifkan kembali workload.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If the maximum TTL value is reached, the workload ends and any remaining "
"queued jobs fail. Any job currently running won't run to completion if doing"
" so would exceed the instance's cost limit.\n"
msgstr ""
"Jika nilai TTL maksimum tercapai, workload berakhir dan semua job yang masih"
" dalam antrean akan gagal. Job yang sedang berjalan tidak akan selesai jika "
"melanjutkannya akan melebihi batas biaya instance.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The following video illustrates the basic workflow, using sessions as an "
"example:\n"
msgstr ""
"Video berikut menggambarkan alur kerja dasar, menggunakan session sebagai "
"contoh:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<IBMVideo id=\"134371940\" title=\"A user starts a session job and becomes "
"the priority user.  They submit jobs to the QPU while other users wait. "
"After the prioritized user's session finishes, the next person's jobs can "
"begin processing.\"/>\n"
msgstr ""
"<IBMVideo id=\"134371940\" title=\"Seorang pengguna memulai job session dan "
"menjadi pengguna prioritas. Mereka mengirimkan job ke QPU sementara pengguna"
" lain menunggu. Setelah session pengguna yang diprioritaskan selesai, job "
"orang berikutnya bisa mulai diproses.\"/>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For full details about the TTL timers, see the [Maximum execution "
"time](/guides/max-execution-time) guide.\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk detail lengkap tentang timer TTL, lihat panduan [Waktu eksekusi "
"maksimum](/guides/max-execution-time).\n"

